BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fine Arts and Artisans Holiday Marketplace
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTSTAMP:20261108T164655Z
UID:7f90c5f759ca34ea18f85f257f0f@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Annual Fine Arts and Artisans Holiday Marketplace November 7&#
 8211\;December 23\, 2026 | Middletown\, Rhode Island Opening Reception Sat
 urday November 7th\, 5:00 - 7:00 PM Holiday Party Saturday December 5th\, 
 5:00 - 7:00 PM Gallery Nights Thursday November 12th and December 10th\, 5
 :00 - 7:00 PM DeBlois Gallery is delighted to present its annual Fine Arts
  and Artisans Marketplace from Nov. 7 &#8211\; Dec. 23\, 2026\, bringing t
 ogether original artwork and handcrafted gifts for the holiday season. Spa
 nning November and December\, the marketplace will offer visitors a two-mo
 nth period to shop for distinctive gifts while supporting local artists an
 d artisans. The diverse selection includes ornaments\, jewelry\, wearable 
 art\, prints\, paintings\, pottery and holiday cards. Fine art and crafts 
 share the gallery space\, offering an inviting mix of pieces to display\, 
 wear\, use and give. For shoppers seeking gifts with a personal connection
 \, the marketplace offers choices ranging from jewelry to suit your indivi
 dual style\, to pottery and original artwork that add an artistic touch to
  your home. There are also hand-crafted holiday ornaments and cards ideal 
 for observing seasonal traditions. DeBlois gift certificates will also be 
 available\, the perfect present for recipients to choose a work that speak
 s to them. As one of Rhode Island’s few cooperative galleries\, DeBlois 
 offers a distinctive setting shaped by the artists who love the space\, br
 inging a variety of creative perspectives into one shared space where visi
 tors can discover different styles and media in a welcoming atmosphere. Th
 e holiday marketplace reflects that spirit\, celebrating individual crafts
 manship and the collective creativity of the gallery community. Participat
 ing artists are available for interviews upon request. Deblois Gallery is 
 located at 134 Aquidneck Avenue in Middletown and is open Wednesday throug
 h Sunday\, from 1:00 - 5:00 PM. All are welcome\, and ample free parking i
 s available. Visit www.debloisgallery.com or follow the gallery on Instagr
 am and Facebook for updates on participating artists and holiday events. M
 edia contact: Michael Day | dr.mday@gmail.com Gallery: (401) 847-9977 | ww
 w.debloisgallery.com Instagram / Facebook\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhod
 eisland.com/event/fine-arts-and-artisans-holiday-marketplace/112555/
LOCATION:DeBlois Gallery\, 134 Aquidneck Avenue\, Middletown\, RI 02842
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/fine-arts-and-artisans-holiday-
 marketplace/112555/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A New England Thanksgiving
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTSTAMP:20261108T164655Z
UID:0706be5d27f4a9d3b565338261a5@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join the Coggeshall staff as we prepare a Thanksgiving meal ov
 er the hearth in our historic farmhouse. The late 18th century was before 
 the official start of Thanksgiving as a national holiday\, but the day was
  still celebrated with food and prayer in New England. Watch our costumed 
 historians make chicken on a string\, bake a pie in the hot coals\, mash t
 urnips and churn butter. In the woodshop we will also demonstrate carving 
 wooden spoons. Explore the garden to see the last of the fall harvest. Wal
 k the nature trail and look for signs of wild turkey\, see musket demonstr
 ations and try your aim with rubber band targets. Please note: This is not
  a Thanksgiving meal for visitors to eat. Food prepared in the historic Fa
 rmhouse Kitchen does not meet modern health and food preparation codes for
  public consumption.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-n
 ew-england-thanksgiving/112116/
LOCATION:Coggeshall Farm Museum\, 1 Colt Drive\, Bristol\, 02809 Time: 10:
 00 AM to 4:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-new-england-thanksgiving/1121
 16/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aurora Skies - Painting Class
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTSTAMP:20261108T164655Z
UID:b81f5be932d1618d2cc7fcfac585@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:🖌️ IN-STUDIO SESSION DETAILS Reserve your spot and enjoy 
 a complimentary beverage—choose from soda\, beer\, or wine (21+ with val
 id ID). Additional drinks will be available for purchase. Immerse yourself
  in a fun and creative atmosphere while painting your own unique masterpie
 ce! Recommended for ages 14 and up. ⏰ ARRIVAL TIME Our studio opens 30 m
 inutes prior to class time. We recommend arriving 15&#8211\;30 minutes ear
 ly to find parking\, grab a drink\, and get settled. Please note: If you a
 rrive late\, the artist may not be able to fill you in on the steps you mi
 ssed\, as they will be focused on guiding the rest of the class. If you ar
 rive more than 20 minutes late\, we kindly ask that you do not join the se
 ssion. Late arrivals can be disruptive and may not have enough time to com
 plete the painting. Unfortunately\, we cannot offer refunds or reschedules
  for late arrivals. 🚗 PARKING INFO Our studio is located at 150 Main St
 reet (rear entrance)\, Pawtucket\, Rhode Island\, and we have two FREE par
 king lots: 🚗 One directly attached to our entrance 🚗 A second lot ju
 st one building down on the same side of the street — clearly labeled 
 🪑 WANT TO SIT WITH FRIENDS? If you purchased 2 or more tickets in one t
 ransaction\, we’ll automatically seat your group together. If you booked
  separately but want to sit with someone\, please include their first and 
 last names in the “Additional Information / Order Notes” field during 
 checkout. 🔄 RESCHEDULING &amp\; CANCELLATION POLICY All reservations ar
 e non-refundable. However\, if you need to reschedule\, you may request a 
 reschedule voucher at least 48 hours before your session. You can do this 
 easily on our website — just [click here]. No-shows cannot be reschedule
 d. 🚨 CLASS CANCELLATION Classes may be canceled due to low attendance. 
 In this case\, we’ll notify you and issue a voucher for a future session
 . We appreciate your understanding and look forward to welcoming you to a 
 future class! ❄️ INCLEMENT WEATHER POLICY Because New England weather 
 can be unpredictable\, we typically wait until a few hours before class to
  make final decisions. If we cancel due to snow or other severe weather\, 
 we’ll email you a voucher for a future session. Have more questions? Che
 ck out our [Frequently Asked Questions] page — just [click here].\n\nSou
 rce: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/aurora-skies-painting-class/11
 2365/
LOCATION:Paint and Vino\, 150 Main Street\, Pawtucket\, RI 02860
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/aurora-skies-painting-class/112
 365/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cars & Coffee — Sachuest Beach (Second Beach)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTSTAMP:20261108T164655Z
UID:65fa512e8a45828f9a67e044fcfd@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Cars &amp\; Coffee When: Select Sundays from 8:00 AM to 10:00 
 AM at Second Beach\, 315 Sachuest Point Road\, Middletown May 10 October 1
 1 October 18 October 25 November 8 November 15 Cars &amp\; Coffee\, hosted
  by the Audrain Automobile Museum\, has grown exponentially since the star
 t - now eight years ago\, only 52 cars appeared at the first event! The Ca
 rs &amp\; Coffee family has expanded\, now consistently seeing 350-400 car
 s on the field and more than 1\,000 at the Motor Week event. We feel that 
 Cars &amp\; Coffee is now the backbone Audrain Automobile Museum and the l
 ocal car community as well. Cheers to another season! Below are a couple r
 eminders for the 2026 Season: For Audrain Members\, registration will open
  the Monday before each of the Cars &amp\; Coffee events and public regist
 ration will open on the Wednesday before each of the Cars &amp\; Coffee ev
 ents. In order to register for one of the Cars &amp\; Coffee events\, you 
 must be subscribed to our email list. You cannot register for any of the C
 ars &amp\; Coffee events through the Audrain website or over the phone. On
 ly Vehicles are required to register for the event. Guests of drivers\, an
 d spectators do not need to register. *All events are subject to change. A
 ll events are rain or shine unless noted.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhod
 eisland.com/event/cars-%26-coffee-%e2%80%94-sachuest-beach-(second-beach)/
 109992/
LOCATION:Sachuest Beach (Second Beach)\, 315 Sachuest Point Rd\, Middletow
 n\, RI 02842 Time: 8:00 AM to 10:00 AM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/cars-%26-coffee-%e2%80%94-sachu
 est-beach-(second-beach)/109992/
END:VEVENT
